import org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils;
public class PadMain {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String s = StringUtils.leftPad("abc", Integer.MIN_VALUE, ' ');
        System.out.println("RESULT=" + s);
        if (!"abc".equals(s)) System.exit(1);
    }
}
JAVA
cd $REPO && git reset --hard <sha> && git clean -fd && mvn -B -q test-compile -Dspotless.check.skip=true -Dcheckstyle.skip=true -Drat.skip=true -Denforcer.skip=true && javac -cp target/classes -d /tmp /tmp/PadMain.java && java -Xmx256m -cp target/classes:/tmp PadMain
At parent_commit this aborts with java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space and a non-zero exit; at fix_commit it prints RESULT=abc and exits 0. The -Xmx cap keeps the OOM fast and deterministic on any host.
